      "text": "To find the value of \\(ab + ac + bc\\), we must utilize Vieta's formulas. Vieta's formulas for a cubic equation \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0\\) provide relations between coefficients and sums involving the roots \\(a, b, c\\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[ 3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8 = 0 \\]\n\nFrom Vieta's formulas, we know:\n1. The sum of the roots \\(a + b + c = -\\frac{b}{a}\\)\n2. The sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time \\(ab + ac + bc = \\frac{c}{a}\\)\n\nTo solve for \\(ab + ac + bc\\), we need:\n\\[ ab + ac + bc = \\frac{c}{a} \\]\n\nGiven the polynomial:\n\\[ 3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8 = 0 \\]\n\nWe identify:\n- \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\) as the roots of the polynomial\n\nAccording to Vieta's formulas:\n- \\(a + b + c = -\\frac{-3}{3} = 1\\)\n\n- \\(ab + ac + bc = \\frac{-8}{3}\\)\n\nThus:\n\\[ ab + ac + bc = \\frac{-8}{3} \\]\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{8}{3}}\n\\]\n\nTechnical math college, Thai's colleges, Technical college, Research centers, universities, Ph.D.s, Masters is easy.\n\nGiven the probability $p = 0.6$ that a distribution on the set $\\{0,1,2,3, \\ldots\\}$ is even, determine the probability that a random variable $\\xi_k$ from this distribution satisfies $\\xi_k \\ge k$.\n\nThe distribution on the set $\\{0,1,2,3, \\ldots\\}$ has probability $p = 0.6$ that a given number in the set is even. We need to determine the probability that a random variable $\\xi_k$ from this distribution satisfies $\\xi_k \\ge k$.\n\nTo do this, we first establish some additional information about the distribution. Since the probabilities are $0.6$ and $0.4$ (for the next higher even number) for each number in the set $\\{n, n+2, \\ldots\\}$, we can infer that the probability of $\\xi_k$ being even is 0.6 and the probability of $\\xi_k$ being odd is 0.4. However, we need more information to directly determine the required probability.\n\nLet's denote the probability that $\\xi_k$ is even by $P(\\xi_k \\text{ is even}) = 0.6$. We need to find the probability that $\\xi_k \\ge k$, which is the probability that $\\xi_k$ is even given that it is at least $k$.\n\nIf $\\xi_k$ is even, it must be one of the even numbers $0, 2, 4, \\ldots, 2m$, where $2m \\ge k$. The probability that $\\xi_k$ is one of these even numbers is the number of even numbers between $0$ and $2m$ divided by the number of even numbers between $0$ and $2k$. This can be expressed as:\n\\[ P(\\xi_k \\text{ is even} \\mid \\xi_k \\ge k) = \\frac{P(\\xi_k \\text{ is even and } \\xi_k \\ge k)}{P(\\xi_k \\ge k)} = \\frac{P(\\xi_k \\text{ is even}) \\cdot P(\\xi_k \\ge k \\mid \\xi_k \\text{ is even})}{P(\\xi_k \\ge k)}. \\]\nSince $P(\\xi_k \\ge k \\mid \\xi_k \\text{ is even}) = 1$, this simplifies to:\n\\[ P(\\xi_k \\text{ is even} \\mid \\xi_k \\ge k) = P(\\xi_k \\text{ is even}). \\]\nTherefore,\n\\[ P(\\xi_k \\ge k) = P(\\xi_k \\text{ is even}) = 0.6. \\]\n\nThus, the probability that a random variable $\\xi_k$ from this distribution satisfies $\\xi_k \\ge k$ is \\(\\boxed{0.6}\\).\n\nSimplify and evaluate $\\cos 15^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ - \\sin 15^\\circ \\sin 150^\\circ$.\n\nTo simplify and evaluate the expression \\(\\cos 15^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ - \\sin 15^\\circ \\sin 150^\\circ\\), we will use trigonometric identities and properties.\n\nFirst, recall the values of the trigonometric functions involved:\n\\[\n\\cos 30^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}, \\quad \\sin 150^\\circ = \\sin (180^\\circ - 30^\\circ) = \\sin 30^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2}.\n\\]\n\nSubstitute these values into the expression:\n\\[\n\\cos 15^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ - \\sin 15^\\circ \\sin 150^\\circ = \\cos 15^\\circ \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} - \\sin 15^\\circ \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}.\n\\]\n\nFactor out \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\):\n\\[\n\\cos 15^\\circ \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} - \\sin 15^\\circ \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{1}{2} (\\cos 15^\\circ \\sqrt{3} - \\sin 15^\\circ).\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the exact values of \\(\\cos 15^\\circ\\) and \\(\\sin 15^\\circ\\). Usi